1
00:00:00,068 --> 00:00:00,908
If you're on X (Twitter),

2
00:00:00,908 --> 00:00:03,028
you probably see 10 new apps every day.

3
00:00:03,145 --> 00:00:05,325
figuring out which one actually works means

4
00:00:05,325 --> 00:00:06,285
giving out your email,

5
00:00:06,685 --> 00:00:07,653
signing up and

6
00:00:07,652 --> 00:00:09,032
figuring them out yourself.

7
00:00:09,038 --> 00:00:10,952
Doing that for every product takes time.

8
00:00:10,952 --> 00:00:10,996
So

9
00:00:10,996 --> 00:00:13,588
I often search YouTube to watch founders use

10
00:00:13,588 --> 00:00:14,347
their own products.

11
00:00:14,691 --> 00:00:16,371
That's why I built TrailScout.

12
00:00:16,371 --> 00:00:18,891
You give an agent a task and it goes and tries the

13
00:00:18,891 --> 00:00:19,891
product for you.

14
00:00:19,946 --> 00:00:22,502
A Scout is the identity an agent uses across

15
00:00:22,582 --> 00:00:22,982
websites.

16
00:00:23,382 --> 00:00:25,022
Each has its own email inbox

17
00:00:25,022 --> 00:00:25,962
through AgentMail.

18
00:00:25,961 --> 00:00:27,059
It remembers its

19
00:00:27,469 --> 00:00:28,829
accounts and how to sign in,

20
00:00:28,829 --> 00:00:31,629
whether with a password or a social login.

21
00:00:31,696 --> 00:00:33,757
Passwords are stored and encrypted using

22
00:00:33,757 --> 00:00:36,457
AES-256-GCM so they're safe.

23
00:00:36,725 --> 00:00:38,826
These scouts are shared across users.

24
00:00:39,012 --> 00:00:40,093
When creating a new task,

25
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:41,573
you can choose between two agents.

26
00:00:41,813 --> 00:00:43,813
OpenAI's Agents API,

27
00:00:43,945 --> 00:00:46,454
with Luna or the Convex Agent component

28
00:00:46,454 --> 00:00:47,067
with Luna,

29
00:00:47,067 --> 00:00:48,349
Qwen or DeepSeek,

30
00:00:48,429 --> 00:00:52,000
I used Luna for most of the reviews because in my

31
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,719
testing it got stuck less often.

32
00:00:53,956 --> 00:00:55,594
Reviews are public by default.

33
00:00:55,594 --> 00:00:57,282
Anyone can read those results.

34
00:00:57,282 --> 00:00:59,962
So one person task can help others decide

35
00:01:00,462 --> 00:01:02,142
whether a product is worth trying.

36
00:01:02,241 --> 00:01:03,601
Now let's give it a task.

37
00:01:03,601 --> 00:01:05,561
I'm asking it to create a Samebase account,

38
00:01:05,561 --> 00:01:07,841
deploy an app and check that it works.

39
00:01:08,242 --> 00:01:09,611
That Involves signup,

40
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:12,402
GitHub and Cloudflare connections and OAuth

41
00:01:12,402 --> 00:01:12,962
authorization.

42
00:01:13,054 --> 00:01:15,445
Firecrawl provides the browser the scout uses.

43
00:01:18,177 --> 00:01:19,805
The agent has a workspace

44
00:01:20,049 --> 00:01:21,975
where it saves files and runs code.

45
00:01:21,974 --> 00:01:23,393
Only admins can see that.

46
00:01:23,578 --> 00:01:24,551
Here opening.

47
00:01:27,376 --> 00:01:27,961
As you can see,

48
00:01:27,961 --> 00:01:29,321
the lab is a bit more complex.

49
00:01:29,322 --> 00:01:31,353
Before an agent actually starts working,

50
00:01:31,513 --> 00:01:33,591
there are a set of reviews that

51
00:01:34,073 --> 00:01:35,673
we do using Fire Crawl

52
00:01:35,673 --> 00:01:38,313
and also every task has its workspace

53
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:40,873
which contains a list of files that the agent can

54
00:01:40,873 --> 00:01:41,832
use for itself.

55
00:01:42,017 --> 00:01:43,936
It can also use Bash and TypeScript.

56
00:01:43,936 --> 00:01:46,501
The main reason for that is that sometimes we get

57
00:01:46,501 --> 00:01:48,783
a very big output from Firecrawl

58
00:01:48,871 --> 00:01:49,272
and

59
00:01:49,561 --> 00:01:50,521
that can mess up

60
00:01:50,521 --> 00:01:52,441
the context window and Compaction even.

61
00:01:52,441 --> 00:01:53,652
the agent can leave

62
00:01:53,972 --> 00:01:54,002
useful,

63
00:01:54,051 --> 00:01:55,131
notes about the site,

64
00:01:55,667 --> 00:01:56,867
in the site's

65
00:01:57,117 --> 00:01:57,917
workspace.

